%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 657659d256d74ba448affc6a2a8763d3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day2_Data
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DaySequenceData
  dayNumber: 2
  steps:
  - stepID: Start
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: Tuesday. The development environment is ready. Today I need to look like someone who knows what to do
      with it.
    displayDuration: 7.4
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Morning_Architect
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Morning_Architect
    speakerName: The Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: Start with one correct tile. Then repeat the rule. A clean design is only useful if we also check that
      it behaves correctly.
    displayDuration: 8.5
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Morning_Pragmatist
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Morning_Pragmatist
    speakerName: The Pragmatist
    personality: 3
    lineText: Or get a grid on the screen before anyone asks questions. We can make it elegant after it works.
    displayDuration: 7.0
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Morning_Detective
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Morning_Detective
    speakerName: The Detective
    personality: 6
    lineText: Steve remembers who we used to be. Watch what he says, and look for familiar details. A little confidence
      might buy us some breathing room.
    displayDuration: 9.3
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_WaitZoom
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_WaitZoom
    speakerName: ''
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 0
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridBrief
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 1
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_GridBrief
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Morning! I started trying to draw a grid after yesterday's SFML setup, but I am not sure how to organize
      the tiles. Could you talk me through how you would approach it? I'd like to understand it before we get to ship
      placement.
    displayDuration: 15.9
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridRequirements
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_GridRequirements
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: For my first attempt, I used eight rows, eight columns, forty-pixel cells, and an origin of one hundred,
      eighty. Would you keep those values together somewhere? I am worried I will have to rewrite the positions if
      the size changes.
    displayDuration: 14.8
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_ChooseApproach
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ChooseApproach
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Where would you start? Could you explain your reasoning so I can follow along?
    displayDuration: 5.2
    choices:
    - choiceText: Let us draw one tile first and make sure we understand its position before duplicating it.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Use row and column numbers to position each tile, instead of choosing every position by hand.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Define the origin, cell size, rows, and columns once, then generate the tiles with nested loops.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Use shared settings and nested loops, then verify the origin, last cell, and loop bounds before
        we call it done.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: Separate grid configuration from drawing, generate from one position rule, and verify both square
        and rectangular dimensions.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect
    - choiceText: I will place the first few squares by eye and copy them until it resembles a grid.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Copy the first row, move each copy down forty pixels, and adjust anything that looks wrong.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use two short loops with eight and forty written directly into them. We can expose settings later.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Make a quick drawing helper, keep the fixed eight-by-eight settings, and check the screenshot.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use a compact loop with adjustable row and column counts. Skip the edge-case tests so we can demo
        immediately.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: We got SFML running yesterday. Let us keep using that setup while I review the grid.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: We already have yesterday's CLion project. Let us keep that environment consistent while I look
        over the implementation.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: You configured SFML through CMakeLists.txt yesterday. Keep that setup in place while I review how
        the grid should fit into it.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: Yesterday you set SFML_DIR for the downloaded library. We can preserve that configuration while
        I decide how to organize the grid.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    - choiceText: You kept SFML under external/ and connected it through CMake yesterday. Let us retain that environment
        while I review the drawing approach.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ChooseApproach_Detective
    nextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_GridTask
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Could I check one calculation with you? For row two, column six, with zero-based indices, forty-pixel
      cells, and origin one hundred, eighty, how would you find the screen position?
    displayDuration: 10.7
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Cell_Architect
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Cell_Architect
    speakerName: The Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: Before answering, ask whether we understand how a grid index becomes a screen position. The more we
      know, the better we can explain and test it.
    displayDuration: 9.6
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Cell_Pragmatist
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Cell_Pragmatist
    speakerName: The Pragmatist
    personality: 3
    lineText: We only need this tile on the screen right now. We can choose how much of the calculation to tidy up
      before the demo.
    displayDuration: 8.9
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Cell_Detective
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Cell_Detective
    speakerName: The Detective
    personality: 6
    lineText: He knows yesterday's SFML setup. Recalling those details might reassure him, but they will not calculate
      this tile's position for us.
    displayDuration: 7.8
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_CellChoice
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_CellChoice
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: How would you explain the position calculation to me?
    displayDuration: 4
    choices:
    - choiceText: Column six should move the tile right, and row two should move it down. Let us check both offsets
        from the origin.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Multiply the column by forty for X and the row by forty for Y, then add the origin.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: X is 100 + 6 * 40 = 340. Y is 80 + 2 * 40 = 160. Use those shared settings for every tile.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Use (340, 160), and test a cell with unequal row and column indices so an axis swap cannot hide.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Use (340, 160). Keep the row-column-to-position conversion in one helper and test it with a different
        origin and cell size too.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Drag the tile until it lines up with the preview. I can adjust it visually.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Set this tile to (340, 160). I will type the remaining positions individually.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use x = 100 + column * 40 and y = 80 + row * 40 directly in this drawing loop.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Put the position calculation in a quick local helper and check this one tile before moving on.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Use the configured origin and size in a short helper. If (2, 6) lines up, ship the preview without
        testing the corners.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Leave the preview open while I check the setup notes from yesterday.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: We can keep the same CLion project from yesterday while I review this position.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: CMake already finds SFML with yesterday's configuration. Keep the build output handy while I review
        the coordinate code.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Your CMake file already links the SFML targets. We can leave that configuration alone while I verify
        the position rule.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Yesterday's library path and linking setup are still relevant. Keep those unchanged; I will review
        the coordinate calculation separately.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_CellChoice_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_CellChoice_Detective
    nextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_CellReview
    speakerName: The Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: A familiar setup detail can make the conversation easier. It cannot replace the position calculation.
      One correct coordinate is useful; a rule that works for every coordinate is better.
    displayDuration: 10.7
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_Exercise_Loops
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ResizeBrief
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: If we changed this from eight by eight to ten by ten, would you update the loops or redraw the tiles?
      I would like to keep the same origin and cell size. How would you handle that change?
    displayDuration: 14.1
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_ResizeChoice
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ResizeChoice
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Which approach would you recommend?
    displayDuration: 4
    choices:
    - choiceText: We need ten rows and ten columns. Let us count the cells instead of only checking the picture.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Change both loop limits to ten and make sure each index stops before ten.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Change the shared rows and columns to ten. The nested loops should then generate one hundred cells
        without copying code.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Update the shared dimensions, check that the count is one hundred, and test the last valid cell
        at row nine, column nine.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Update the configuration, test ten by ten, then six by ten. Verify the count, corners, and that
        each loop uses its own dimension.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Copy more squares around the outside until the larger grid looks full.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Copy two more rows and columns, then move anything that overlaps.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Replace the two hardcoded eights with tens and rerun the same drawing code.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Expose row and column counts in the quick helper, resize to ten by ten, and do one visual check.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Regenerate from the new dimensions, confirm there are one hundred cells, and leave the other sizes
        for tomorrow.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: We can keep using yesterday's SFML window while I review the resize.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Getting that first window open yesterday gave us a starting point. Keep the same project while I
        look at the new size.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: The CMake setup from yesterday should stay as it is. I will review the drawing changes separately.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: The SFML library configuration can stay unchanged while we prepare the larger preview. I will come
        back to the grid dimensions.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Keep the external/ library folder and yesterday's CMake configuration in place. I will review the
        requested dimensions separately from the build setup.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ResizeChoice_Detective
    nextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_GridReview
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: I think I swapped the axes in another version of the helper. Row two, column six appears at one hundred
      eighty, three hundred twenty. Could you help me understand what I got wrong and how you would check the fix?
    displayDuration: 14.8
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_ReviewChoice
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ReviewChoice
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: What would you suggest I change or test?
    displayDuration: 4
    choices:
    - choiceText: Moving across columns should change X. Let us check whether the row and column values were swapped.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: 'Swap the formula inputs: column controls X, and row controls Y.'
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Correct the shared formula to x = originX + column * size and y = originY + row * size; this cell
        should be (340, 160).
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Fix the shared conversion and test (0, 0), (2, 6), and the last valid row and column.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Fix the shared conversion, test unequal dimensions and a changed origin, and verify that neighboring
        cells differ by exactly one cell size on the expected axis.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Architect
    - choiceText: Move the wrong-looking tile into place by hand for now.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Swap the two displayed values for this tile and patch any other visible mistakes.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Swap the row and column in the drawing loop, check this tile, and move on.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Fix the helper, check this cell and the origin, then get the demo ready.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Fix the shared conversion and check the known failing cell. Record the remaining edge tests as follow-up
        work.
      personality: 3
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Pragmatist
    - choiceText: Let us keep yesterday's working setup and note this coordinate issue for another pass.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective_Novice
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: We got the SFML window running yesterday. Keep that setup intact while we put the coordinate issue
        on the review list.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective_Beginner
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 1
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Keep the library configuration we checked yesterday. We can separate the coordinate review from
        changes to the build setup.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective_Intermediate
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 2
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: The setup details from yesterday are still in place. Note the coordinate problem, and I will schedule
        a focused review of that helper.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective_Advanced
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 3
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective
    - choiceText: Retain yesterday's SFML path and linking configuration. I will review the coordinate helper separately
        before we depend on it for board work.
      personality: 6
      targetStepOnClick: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective_Expert
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 4
      choiceGroup: Day2_ReviewChoice_Detective
    nextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_Complete
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: I submitted today's grid. Familiar details helped me manage Steve's suspicion, but tomorrow the code
      will have to stand on its own. Any shortcuts I left in place may still need work.
    displayDuration: 11.9
    choices: []
    nextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: Day_2_Complete
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Novice
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Starting with one tile sounds manageable. Could you show me how you decide where it goes?
    displayDuration: 5.9
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridTask
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Beginner
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: 'I think I follow: one rule for every tile. How would you write that calculation?'
    displayDuration: 5.6
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridTask
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
  - stepID: Day2_ChooseApproach_Architect_Intermediate
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: So the loops use the settings instead of a list of positions? Could you show me how those pieces fit
      together?
    displayDuration: 7.8
    choices: []
    nextStepID: Day2_GridTask
    awardSkillKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
